From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sisyphus <sisyphus@ohmyopencode.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bundled: add missing linux/time_types.h for kernel < 5.8

strace 7.0 bundled taskstats.h includes <linux/time_types.h> but the
file is missing from the bundled headers. On kernel < 5.8 the system
does not provide this header either, causing a build failure.

Add a minimal time_types.h with the definitions needed by taskstats.h
(struct __kernel_timespec and struct __kernel_itimerspec). Omit the
legacy timeval/timespec structures that depend on __kernel_old_time_t,
a type not available in kernel < 5.8.

Signed-off-by: Sisyphus <sisyphus@ohmyopencode.com>
---
 bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h

diff --git a/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h b/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a5b3c1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note */
+#ifndef _UAPI_LINUX_TIME_TYPES_H
+#define _UAPI_LINUX_TIME_TYPES_H
+
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+struct __kernel_timespec {
+	__kernel_time64_t       tv_sec;
+	long long               tv_nsec;
+};
+
+struct __kernel_itimerspec {
+	struct __kernel_timespec it_interval;
+	struct __kernel_timespec it_value;
+};
+
+#endif /* _UAPI_LINUX_TIME_TYPES_H */
